  "notes": "USAGE:\n{規定|きてい} refers to specific rules or clauses within a larger system of regulations. Compare with {規則|きそく} (rules in general, often for everyday conduct), {法律|ほうりつ} (law), and {規約|きやく} (terms, bylaws). {規定|きてい} tends to appear in formal and legal contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {規定|きてい}に{従|したが}う: to follow regulations\n- {規定|きてい}を{設|もう}ける: to establish a regulation\n- {規定|きてい}{違反|いはん}: violation of a regulation\n- {規定|きてい}どおり: as prescribed/stipulated\n- {服務|ふくむ}{規定|きてい}: service regulations",
